.TH ASCIITEST 1
.SH NAME
asciitest \- regression test for ascii(1)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B asciitest
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Asciitest
loads
.BR /p9/dis/ascii.dis 's
in-process test seam,
.BR run(argv) ,
and checks it against a real, live oracle: plan9port's own
.B ascii
binary, run through this emu's host-command-execution device
.RB ( #C ,
see
.IR cmd (3)),
with identical arguments on both sides. Simpler than most of this
backlog's own test suites - ascii(1) needs no host files, only argv in
and stdout out.
.PP
Every case masks the one documented, confirmed
.BR ff / np
label divergence (see
.IR ascii (1)'s
own BUGS) before comparing, so it never hides a REAL divergence behind
a general tolerance rule - only that one specific, already-understood
byte sequence is substituted.
.SH SOURCE
.B /p9/cmd/asciitest.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR ascii (1)
.SH BUGS
Does not exercise a file-argument-as-input case (ascii(1) has none -
every operand is treated as literal text or a code, never a filename),
nor extreme base values beyond a couple of representative ones (2, 8,
10, 16, 36).
